{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell","id":1040435,"title":"[2E] Is it Lasting spell?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T22:30:36-08:00","id":1040435,"title":"[2E] Is it Lasting spell?","content":"Topic for claryfing particular spells. On last game session, we talked is Psychic Reprogramming from Mind 4 just Lasting - as it does not have Lasting option on Reach. What do you think on that? In my POV it should be, beacuse what would it be change for Virtue &amp; Vice from Reprogramming, if you would return to starting one in number of hours or days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:36:44-08:00","id":1040438,"title":"","content":"This is definitely not Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:40:00-08:00","id":1040442,"title":"","content":"I assume that any spell with Potency for Primary Factor that does not explicitly say that it expires after its Duration runs out is a Lasting spell, just to keep it simple.<br /> <br /> Which Psychic Programming... is, now that I've re-checked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:50:57-08:00","id":1040446,"title":"","content":"Lasting is the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> It's reserved for side-effects (the house you burned down with magic fire doesn't come back when the magic goes away), healing (non-regenerative), damage, and +2 Reach options on appropriate spells.<br /> <br /> To clarify - Damage is lasting because the actual spell is to do something that would damage an enemy. After the spell goes away, they're no longer <i>being</i> hurt, but the hurt remains as part of the Pattern's natural state.<br /> <br /> Same for healing - the actual magic is to 'make the body heal this'. Once the spell ends, the user is no longer healing, but the damage they healed remains as a lasting part of their Pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Clarity 01-30-2017, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:01:25-08:00","id":1040451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040446#post1040446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting is the exception, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that makes sense, after looking at some other Potency-primary spells.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:20:20-08:00","id":1040524,"title":"","content":"Psychic Reprogramming isn't Lasting, and that's deliberate. In Mage if you want something to stick then more often than not you have to sink significant resources into it.<br /> <br /> The lack of a Reach option for Lasting should have been your first clue <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:07:57-08:00","id":1040544,"title":"","content":"If it's not explicitly non lasting ST can allow for it to be lasting with Reach effect. If your cool with this spell being lasting - go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:16:35-08:00","id":1040551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040544#post1040544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not explicitly non lasting ST can allow for it to be lasting with Reach effect. If your cool with this spell being lasting - go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If coming back from the dead doesn't get a pass I don't know why having your mind rewritten would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:27:05-08:00","id":1040554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040551#post1040551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If coming back from the dead doesn't get a pass I don't know why having your mind rewritten would.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it's RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making a spell Lasting always costs +2 Reach, but you<br /> should think carefully before allowing it \u2014 only spells<br /> without any way to revert them should have the option. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:30:26-08:00","id":1040555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040554#post1040554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because it's RAW.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's for Creative Thaum. Published spells that have an option to be made Lasting have that option included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:16:00-08:00","id":1040572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040555#post1040555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for Creative Thaum. Published spells that have an option to be made Lasting have that option included.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would agree with this that published spells are outside the Creative Thaumaturgy structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:27:53-08:00","id":1040580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040555#post1040555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for Creative Thaum. Published spells that have an option to be made Lasting have that option included.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree. Every spell that doesn't need magic to be sustained can be made lasting if ST allows. <br /> <br /> Why should Mind Wipe be lasting but not Psychic Reprograming? It's silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040572#post1040572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would agree with this that published spells are outside the Creative Thaumaturgy structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not outside - they are part of Creative T. as an inspirations and examples of mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:28:11-08:00","id":1040581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040572#post1040572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would agree with this that published spells are outside the Creative Thaumaturgy structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really &quot;outside&quot; Creative Thaumaturgy, publishes spells are basically examples for spells created with the Creative Thaumaturgy system. At least that is the intention. So if a published spell doesn't have lasting, the writer explicitely thought, that the spell shouldn't be lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:38:08-08:00","id":1040584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040580#post1040580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Every spell that doesn't need magic to be sustained can be made lasting...</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychic Programming does require magic to be sustained though. Like any gross transformation of a target's inherent nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:40:31-08:00","id":1040585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040581#post1040581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really &quot;outside&quot; Creative Thaumaturgy, publishes spells are basically examples for spells created with the Creative Thaumaturgy system. At least that is the intention. So if a published spell doesn't have lasting, the writer explicitely thought, that the spell shouldn't be lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this. They literally went through and removed Lasting from loads of spells in the errata pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:43:30-08:00","id":1040590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040580#post1040580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree. Every spell that doesn't need magic to be sustained can be made lasting if ST allows.<br /> <br /> Why should Mind Wipe be lasting but not Psychic Reprograming? It's silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They are not outside - they are part of Creative T. as an inspirations and examples of mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The St can change that is a given, The ST can change anything in his game, I reiterate Anything. Creative Thaumaturgy is there to pick up the slack and the published spells shouldn't be changed, When changing a published spell it in now a custom spell under the rules of Creative Thaumaturgy, Now that it is under the Creative Thaumaturgy it is not the same spell as the published one and therefore is no longer a Rote or Praxis if there were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:51:07-08:00","id":1040594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040580#post1040580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should Mind Wipe be lasting but not Psychic Reprograming? It's silly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because the former is a spell to destroy memory by going in and removing them. Its no different than using a spell to cut off a finger, versus using a spell to shapeshift a hand into claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:59:27-08:00","id":1040602,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind there are guidelines for Creative Thaum-ing published spells. For example, changing just Primary Factor is a no-no. It is reasonable to conclude that just adding a Reach effect that was intentionally excluded when the spell was written would be disallowed as well. Especially because, as I mentioned before, they explicitly went through and <i>removed</i> a lot of Lasting effects in the errata. That was a conscious choice on the part of the developers, and differs from adding something they just might not have thought of (eg. a Reach Effect for Speak with the Dead allowing you to speak with Mages in Death Twilight)<br /> <br /> That said, it Creative Thaumaturgy does encourage a degree of messing with published spells - the system encourages you to try to accomplish effects with alternate Arcana, but if you want a Lasting effect on a non-Lasting spell you need to reimagine how the spell accomplishes its goals, in a way that is compatible with the rules regarding what spells should be Lasting.<br /> <br /> A good example of how to envision things like this is Ghost Gate. The default, portal-style spell is designed in such a way that the effect would (arguably, lets not have that argument here) be Lasting. The spell creates a portal that shifts things that pass through it into Twilight. When the spell ends, the portal goes away. The side effects of the spell (things that went through are in Twilight) do not, just as the ground a fire burns doesn't become unburnt when the magical fire goes away.<br /> <br /> The reach effect works completely differently - it directly shifts a subject into Twilight, so when the spell ends, the subject would cease being in Twilight.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a non-Lasting spell Lasting, the process should be more in-depth than just slapping on two Reach and calling it good. Figure out how to accomplish the same effect in a Lasting manner, and do that. Sometimes the result will be an alteration of the published spell, sometimes it will be something brand new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-30-2017, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:10:31-08:00","id":1040608,"title":"","content":"Here, Here and amen to that, I totally agree with this. That is why I stated that the spell would be a different spell if you started to monkey with it using the Creative Thaumaturgy rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:12:34-08:00","id":1040610,"title":"","content":"Sever Oaths that modifies Destiny Merit, Soul Jar which bounds soul to anything, Alter Integrity that adds durability, Hallow Dance, Cut Threads which severs sympathy at 4 dots, Create Sympathy, Shifting Sands, Corridors of Time are all Lasting. <br /> <br /> Published spells are not finished or 'closed'. If you think that you can squeze some juice out of them you should do it by adding Reach.<br /> <br /> What spells are lasting is up to a setting and that's why Deny the Reaper is explicitly non-lasting. It's up to ST to figure out what he want's. That said I wouldn't <i>personally </i>allow for with Psychic Reprograming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:19:44-08:00","id":1040613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040608#post1040608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, Here and amen to that, I totally agree with this. That is why I stated that the spell would be a different spell if you started to monkey with it using the Creative Thaumaturgy rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, they wouldn't... If you add a Reach effect to Memory Hole that lets you replace a memory with a fake one you're not changing a spell. You are just a skilled magician.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:20:44-08:00","id":1040615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040610#post1040610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sever Oaths that modifies Destiny Merit, Soul Jar which bounds soul to anything, Alter Integrity that adds durability, Hallow Dance, Cut Threads which severs sympathy at 4 dots, Create Sympathy, Shifting Sands, Corridors of Time are all Lasting.<br /> <br /> Published spells are not finished or 'closed'. If you think that you can squeze some juice out of them you should do it by adding Reach.<br /> <br /> What spells are lasting is up to a setting and that's why Deny the Reaper is explicitly non-lasting. It's up to ST to figure out what he want's. That said I wouldn't <i>personally </i>allow for with Psychic Reprograming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would partially agree, squeeze the juice out of it with published compatible reaches. The ones that can be applied to any spell is Potency, Duration, Scale, Range, and Casting Time all others that would be allowed to change a spell is listed with that spell. To add anything else needs to be Creative Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:23:22-08:00","id":1040616,"title":"","content":"That reach is not listed as a Published reach for that spell and therefore it would require Creative Thaumaturgy to change the Published spell parameters.<br /> <br /> Memory Hole (Mind \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Medicine, Subterfuge<br /> The mage compartmentalizes the subject\u2019s thoughts, placing<br /> memories into areas that she cannot access or remember.<br /> The mage can compartmentalize one memory per Potency,<br /> making the subject forget them completely for the Duration<br /> of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:24:34-08:00","id":1040617,"title":"","content":"The issue with adding Lasting to published spells is that all of the writers had that as an option. They used it where they felt it was appropriate, to the point that the devs then had to go through and <i>remove </i>instances where it was used incorrectly.<br /> <br /> It is <i>very</i> reasonable to operate on the understanding that, among the published spells, if it's meant to be Lasting, or to have a Reach for it, it does. Some spells are described in a way that they <i>would</i> have Lasting effects without actually saying they're Lasting. See Ghost Gate, Shaping, Corridors of Time.<br /> <br /> Others have the Reach for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-30-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:29:07-08:00","id":1040619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040616#post1040616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reach is not listed as a Published reach for that spell and therefore it would require Creative Thaumaturgy to change the Published spell parameters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with C.T. i that it is part of magic system. <br /> <br /> So look here and tell me why Memory Hole shouldn't have this option.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Chronos (Time \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Stealth, Subterfuge</b><br /> The mage shields a subject against temporal senses. While<br /> under the protection of this spell, any magic viewing the subject<br /> through time (whether looking at the shielded Duration from<br /> the future, or predicting the subject\u2019s future while in the present)<br /> provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: Instead of simply preventing magic from uncovering<br /> the subject during the Duration of the shield, the mage may<br /> design a false series of events that inquisitive powers \u201cuncover\u201d<br /> instead of the truth. Attempts to magically discern the illusion<br /> provoke a Clash of Wills.</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:33:18-08:00","id":1040622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040617#post1040617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is <i>very</i> reasonable to operate on the understanding that, among the published spells, if it's meant to be Lasting, or to have a Reach for it, it does. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that you should do it carefully to not 'break' a game and I wouldn't do it with this spell <i>but </i>it's up to a ST. I think that we just should agree to disagree here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:36:22-08:00","id":1040624,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> spells that allow you to go back in time are not Lasting. The things that you change as a result of going back are Lasting because they're side effects of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:39:35-08:00","id":1040625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040619#post1040619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing with C.T. i that it is part of magic system.<br /> <br /> So look here and tell me why Memory Hole shouldn't have this option.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Chronos (Time \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Stealth, Subterfuge</b><br /> The mage shields a subject against temporal senses. While<br /> under the protection of this spell, any magic viewing the subject<br /> through time (whether looking at the shielded Duration from<br /> the future, or predicting the subject\u2019s future while in the present)<br /> provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: Instead of simply preventing magic from uncovering<br /> the subject during the Duration of the shield, the mage may<br /> design a false series of events that inquisitive powers \u201cuncover\u201d<br /> instead of the truth. Attempts to magically discern the illusion<br /> provoke a Clash of Wills.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned above, there's a meaningful difference between adding Reach effects the writes may not have thought of, and adding a Reach effect that is explicitly a core part of the system and intentionally rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:44:08-08:00","id":1040627,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I know. Shaping can make fantastic shapes that are lasting, Shifting Sands rewrites history and Psychic reprograming can't leave a person behind that is totally fine, just different then before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:46:35-08:00","id":1040628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040627#post1040627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I know. Shaping can make fantastic shapes that are lasting, Shifting Sands rewrites history and Psychic reprograming can't leave a person behind that is totally fine, just different then before?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not accurate, though. Shaping gives you the ability to shape matter. When the spell ends, that ability ends with it. The things you DID are lasting effects.<br /> Shifting Sands isn't lasting either - again, it's the side effects that are a result of what you did while under the effect of the spell that are Lasting.<br /> <br /> The sidebar on Lasting explains this stuff fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:48:03-08:00","id":1040630,"title":"","content":"So, just to ask, Monkey\u2019s Paw (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) would last for how many time? It has Potency as primary factor. It's duration is 1 turn? 1 use? Or lasting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:49:11-08:00","id":1040631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040619#post1040619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing with C.T. i that it is part of magic system.<br /> <br /> So look here and tell me why Memory Hole shouldn't have this option.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Chronos (Time \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Stealth, Subterfuge</b><br /> The mage shields a subject against temporal senses. While<br /> under the protection of this spell, any magic viewing the subject<br /> through time (whether looking at the shielded Duration from<br /> the future, or predicting the subject\u2019s future while in the present)<br /> provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: Instead of simply preventing magic from uncovering<br /> the subject during the Duration of the shield, the mage may<br /> design a false series of events that inquisitive powers \u201cuncover\u201d<br /> instead of the truth. Attempts to magically discern the illusion<br /> provoke a Clash of Wills.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That isn't memory Hole that is a different spell, so i don't get the point that you are trying to make here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:49:17-08:00","id":1040632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040625#post1040625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned above, there's a meaningful difference between adding Reach effects the writes may not have thought of, and adding a Reach effect that is explicitly a core part of the system and intentionally rare.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why I directed this Shield of Chronos to Hardwire, not you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Lasting Reach effect is explicitly a core part of the system and intentionally rare<i> but possible and up to ST who should be careful.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:54:07-08:00","id":1040634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040632#post1040632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's why I directed this Shield of Chronos to Hardwire, not you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Lasting Reach effect is explicitly a core part of the system and intentionally rare<i> but possible and up to ST who should be careful.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And all I am trying to say if if you want to add lasting, then by all means add lasting, but it isn't the published spell any more. It was mutated by Creative Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:54:09-08:00","id":1040635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040630#post1040630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just to ask, Monkey\u2019s Paw (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) would last for how many time? It has Potency as primary factor. It's duration is 1 turn? 1 use? Or lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Turn unless you raise duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:58:23-08:00","id":1040636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040628#post1040628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not accurate, though. Shaping gives you the ability to shape matter. When the spell ends, that ability ends with it. The things you DID are lasting effects.<br /> Shifting Sands isn't lasting either - again, it's the side effects that are a result of what you did while under the effect of the spell that are Lasting.<br /> <br /> The sidebar on Lasting explains this stuff fairly well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um. Maybe I'm expressing this in a hazy way but I DO KNOW whats the difference between spell and it's effect. Look at this: + 2 Reach: Rather then forcufully anddirectly changing subjects personality the caster can now toy with subjects personality with his own thoughts for the duration of the spell. After that changes set and are lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:00:38-08:00","id":1040639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040630#post1040630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just to ask, Monkey\u2019s Paw (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) would last for how many time? It has Potency as primary factor. It's duration is 1 turn? 1 use? Or lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know why but this question feels kinda aggressive. It's 1 Turn of duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:02:49-08:00","id":1040642,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Shield of Chronos Reach effect is lasting. As I read it, when someone tries to use Postcognition (or a similar power) on the shielded area, they bypass the Shield if they win the CoW, or see that that timeframe is Veiled if they lose. What the Reach effect does is to present them a false lead instead of noticing the target is Veiled, *in case they lose the CoW*.<br /> <br /> This opens up a few questions on *when* the target needs to be Shielded, but that's not for this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:04:49-08:00","id":1040644,"title":"","content":"Once again I think she was trying to point out the a reach from one spell should be able to work with another spell of similar ability. No that it was lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:07:24-08:00","id":1040648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040642#post1040642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Shield of Chronos Reach effect is lasting. As I read it, when someone tries to use Postcognition (or a similar power) on the shielded area, they bypass the Shield if they win the CoW, or see that that timeframe is Veiled if they lose. What the Reach effect does is to present them a false lead instead of noticing the target is Veiled, *in case they lose the CoW*.<br /> <br /> This opens up a few questions on *when* the target needs to be Shielded, but that's not for this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not Lasting. Veiling is a purely magical effect which doesn't change subject and can't be maintained without magic. I brought it to compare it with Memory Hole for the sake of 'adding reach changes spell into monstrosity' part of conversation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:11:32-08:00","id":1040649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040630#post1040630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just to ask, Monkey\u2019s Paw (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) would last for how many time? It has Potency as primary factor. It's duration is 1 turn? 1 use? Or lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's default Duration is 1 Turn. Potency is better because it can jack up the equipment bonus, so it's the Primary Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:14:15-08:00","id":1040650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040627#post1040627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I know. Shaping can make fantastic shapes that are lasting, Shifting Sands rewrites history and Psychic reprograming can't leave a person behind that is totally fine, just different then before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike Shaping or Time travel spells Psychic Programming is significantly altering the fundamental nature of the subject. It's closer to Transubstantiation from Matter, or Shapechange from Life than it is to Shaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:31:12-08:00","id":1040657,"title":"","content":"I would generally allow the storyteller option of making the spell Lasting with +2 Reach if the character demonstrates, how will they create the spell effect in a way that uses Exoteric knowledge to effectively make *the effect as described* a side effect.<br /> <br /> For example, if you use Life 3 to give yourself a tail, it's normally not Lasting. But if the mage would, say, use Life 2 to change individual nucleotides and genes in human genome (the side effect) by manipulating various enzymes in human body (the spell effect itself), I would rule it's Lasting. Of course, you would need to know what sequences you need (whether you use magic to figure that out or not is not relevant, so use those Fate and Time spells as much as you like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":".  Changed the Life practice needed for the tail. 01-30-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:33:18-08:00","id":1040658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040650#post1040650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unlike Shaping or Time travel spells Psychic Programming is significantly altering the fundamental nature of the subject. It's closer to Transubstantiation from Matter, or Shapechange from Life than it is to Shaping.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Shapechange makes a dog with cognitive abilities of a human and that is impossible to find in nature, Psychic Reprogramming leaves a person. Different but still a person. I understand why it's not lasting by default and I wouldn't allow it to be lasting. But still, I believe it's up to a ST.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about Transform Life is that it can be past to offsprings. Maybe Shapechange could do it too?(lets don't go in there in this thread)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-30-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:35:32-08:00","id":1040660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040657#post1040657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would generally allow the storyteller option of making the spell Lasting with +2 Reach if the character demonstrates, how will they create the spell effect in a way that uses Exoteric knowledge to effectively make *the effect as described* a side effect.<br /> <br /> For example, if you use Life 4 to give yourself a tail, it's normally not Lasting. But if the mage would, say, use Life 2 to change individual nucleotides and genes in human genome (the side effect) by manipulating various enzymes in human body (the spell effect itself), I would rule it's Lasting. Of course, you would need to know what sequences you need (whether you use magic to figure that out or not is not relevant, so use those Fate and Time spells as much as you like).</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be Life 3. Other then that I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:13:30-08:00","id":1040673,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. That's what I get from skimming the conversation, I guess. Sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:04:19-08:00","id":1040701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1040636#post1040636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Maybe I'm expressing this in a hazy way but I DO KNOW whats the difference between spell and it's effect. Look at this: + 2 Reach: Rather then forcufully anddirectly changing subjects personality the caster can now toy with subjects personality with his own thoughts for the duration of the spell. After that changes set and are lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Reach effect doesn't actually explain <i>why</i> the effects are Lasting. Changing thoughts isn't described as a side effect of the magic. It <i>is</i> the magic, even in this spell. Still, if it works for you, use it.<br /> <br /> I'd advise, however, instead of bolting on a Reach effect, consider other ways to accomplish the goal, re-imagining an effect that actually cooperates with the description of how Lasting effects are inflicted:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Fungible Psyche (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Ski</b>lls: Academics, Expression, Persuasion<br /> The mage is capable of sending subjects into a fragile state of mind, where they allow the external world to shape their self-identity. This spell inflicts the Impressionable Condition on the subject, which remains for the Duration of the spell, or until the subject resolves it normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The subject instead gains the Hypnotic Trance Condition<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Impressionable</b><br /> Your character's psyche has been made supernaturally plastic, and you take all of your cues from the world around you instead of looking inward. Any time another character involved in the same scenes fulfills their Virtue or Vice, gaining Willpower from it, replace your Virtue or Vice with their own. If another character involved in a scene with you discusses meaningful plans to move towards a given Aspiration or Obsession, replace your oldest Aspiration or Obsession with the one being discussed. This effect continues, layering replacement after replacement, until this Condition is resolved, leaving the character with a seemingly stable identity.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Suffer a breaking point as a result of actions taken due to Aspirations or Obsessions gained from this Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Hypnotic Trance</b><br /> Your character's psyche has been made supernaturally plastic, to the point that anyone remotely persuasive or charismatic can mold you into whatever they desire. This functions as Impressionable, but in addition to the effects listed above, anyone aware of your vulnerable state can mold your mind with a simple, uncontested social roll describing the benefits of a given Virtue or Vice, or detailing why a particular Aspiration or Obsession is worth pursuing. This roll may use Presence or Manipulation, and either Persuasion, Intimidation, or Expression as is appropriate to their approach. Success changes the relevant trait as if it had been witnessed in action, per Impressionable.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Suffer a breaking point as a result of actions taken due to Aspirations or Obsessions gained from this Condition. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This effect of this spell puts someone into a state of mind where they can be so easily influenced it actually changes their in-game traits, instead of just brazenly overwriting them via magic directly. As a result, when the effect ends, the Conditions expire...but the traits that changed as a result are still altered. It's neater, plays nice with the thematics of how Lasting effects are supposed to work, and actually costs less reach than the bolt-on effect.<br /> <br /> I'd have written up something for the stat-swapping portion of Psychic Reprogramming, but I think that part is even easier to approach creatively, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:32:50-08:00","id":1040717,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> I love it. Steeling of course. I guess my Reach option was a try at achieving something like Telepathic link while the target is in Hypnotic Trance. You take is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:55:27-08:00","id":1040801,"title":"","content":"Nice spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:20:33-08:00","id":1041663,"title":"","content":"I think the main reason they took the Lasting Reach effects out is because they didn't want those powerful effects to be in the default state of the game, not because they couldn't be allowed by your ST if he so chooses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:13:02-08:00","id":1041708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040435-2e-is-it-lasting-spell?p=1041663#post1041663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main reason they took the Lasting Reach effects out is because they didn't want those powerful effects to be in the default state of the game, not because they couldn't be allowed by your ST if he so chooses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they took them out because they didn't match the sidebar describing what should be Lasting. Regardless, anything can be allowed by your ST, discussions built around that can't really go anywhere.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}